-- title:
--   Étale coordinate at a rational point over a DVR
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, and let $\varpi \in A$ be an element generating its maximal ideal. Let $B$ be a formally smooth, finitely presented $A$-algebra such that the image $\varpi_B$ of $\varpi$ in $B$ is a prime element, and such that the quotient $B/\varpi_B B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. Let $\mathfrak n \subset B$ be a maximal ideal with $\varpi_B \in \mathfrak n$ and $\mathfrak n \neq \varpi_B B$, and assume that the composite $A \to B \to B/\mathfrak n$ is surjective, so that the residue field at $\mathfrak n$ is the residue field of $A$. Let $S$ be a commutative $B$-algebra which is local and is a localisation of $B$ at the prime $\mathfrak n$. Then there exists $t \in \mathfrak n$ such that the maximal ideal of $S$ is generated by the images in $S$ of $\varpi_B$ and of $t$, and such that the evaluation homomorphism $A[X] \to S$ over the composite $A \to B \to S$ sending $X$ to the image of $t$ is formally smooth, formally unramified, and essentially of finite type.
--
--   This is the statement that a smooth relative curve over a discrete valuation ring is, locally at a rational point of its special fibre, étale over the affine line $\mathbb A^1_A$, with $(\varpi, t)$ a regular system of parameters of the two-dimensional regular local ring $S$. It is used in the analysis of the local rings of modular curves at supersingular points, in the construction of the prolongation of the supersingular locus over affine charts of the full-level modular curve.
